00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:04.080
I suppose you can do better.

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:04.880
Anytime.

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:07.720
Everybody says I make the best fried chicken in the valley.

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.020
I never said it.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:13.170
Ladies, wouldn't you like to settle this like gentlemen?

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:27.050
What do you think of our neighbors now?

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:29.710
I'll let you know after I've counted the silver.

00:20:32.110 --> 00:20:35.830
Lisa, can you imagine all those men coming here and helping me plow my fields?

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:39.530
And all those women spending all morning in the kitchen cooking chicken.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:41.730
Yeah, I don't think you should have asked them to cook after the men did all.

00:20:41.730 --> 00:20:43.190
Oh, darling, I didn't ask them.

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:44.040
Why did they do it?

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:46.370
I had a chicken cooking contest.

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:46.750
A what?

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:49.250
I borrowed the idea from Mr. Carson.

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:51.850
You didn't ask them for an entry fee.

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:54.480
Oh, no, I offered them a price.

00:20:55.970 --> 00:20:59.450
Mr. Douglas, we thank you very much.

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:00.000
Who knows?

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.660
Our pleasure. Thank you, Mr. Miller.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:02.920
Bye, sir.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.400
Come back again soon.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:05.760
Bye, Mr. Miller.

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:08.910
Lisa, what did you...

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:10.470
Wait a second, that's our couch!

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:11.650
No, darling.

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:13.990
That is the first rise.
